{"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_019TgdE1v65CKcZg2uCqMfHU","input":{"command":"git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nImplement MVP: cross-CLI resume with native session fabrication\n\nTurnbridge is the resume layer over conversation-ledger (which owns capture).\n`turnbridge resume [claude|codex]` lists conversations compatible with the\ncurrent repo/HEAD, filtered to the current git-identity author by default\n(--all for collaborators), then hands off to the target CLI:\n\n- same-CLI picks use native resume;\n- cross-CLI picks fabricate a target-native session file (Claude .jsonl /\n  Codex rollout) so the target's own resume loads it, verified against\n  claude 2.1.x and codex-cli 0.144.x; Codex fabrication emits event_msg\n  display twins so the TUI scrollback renders, not just model context;\n- --bootstrap (and automatic fallback) rehydrates via a literal transcript\n  file the fresh session is told to read.\n\nBridging forks a conversation, so a `continuation` ledger event records\nsource->target lineage; the picker labels both directions and warns on\nre-bridge. Includes opt-in PATH shims, a saved default-target flow, and the\nreverse-engineered format specs under docs/specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -3","description":"Commit turnbridge MVP implementation"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"49da723e6046dbccfcf0e3966f6e68a44a5964dd","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-422b80b2b3752a78f90a06d0253fbac0c0b1953816e7c6a462cc42acfb686a45","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-4-8","type":"agent"},"session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code"},"occurred_at":"2026-07-19T17:07:38.787Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.2.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effor