{"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01V963HgseDFKxq4Tv8UC2bC","input":{"content":"# Context Graph\n\nA navigable graph of how everything in a repository connects — code, docs, and\nconversations, as one heterogeneous graph.\n\nMost of what a repository knows lives in the connections between its artifacts:\na file imports another, a doc explains a module, a conversation decides why a\nline is the way it is, a commit implements that decision. Those relationships\nexist but are never written down as first-class, addressable structure. Context\nGraph makes them explicit — typed edges, each traceable to the evidence that\njustifies it.\n\nThe first artifacts it wires up are **conversations**, because\n[Conversation Ledger](https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger)\nalready stores them durably and turnbridge already writes lineage edges into\nit. Code and doc nodes follow, sharing one identifier namespace so a\nconversation and the file it discusses are joinable.\n\nThis repository is intentionally at the design stage. Nothing here is locked\nin — it records current impressions and the shape of the problem, not a\ncommitted API. See [product intent](docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md) and the\n[WIP technical design](docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md).\n\n## Where it sits\n\n- **conversation-ledger** — neutral, immutable store of conversation events;\n  the first source Context Graph reads.\n- **turnbridge** — captures/moves conversations between CLIs; already writes\n  `continuation` lineage edges into the ledger for this tool to surface.\n- **intent-recall** — reads the ledger to answer \"what was intended?\"; a\n  sibling consumer, not a dependency.\n- **context-graph** (this repo) — derives the explicit relationship graph over\n  the ledger now, and over code/docs as extractors are added.\n- **[tagseq2tagseq](https://github.com/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq)** — trains\n  language models by traversing a text-attributed document graph; the natural\n  downstream consumer of the graph this tool emits (see the design doc).\n\n## License\n\n[MIT](LICENSE)\n","file_path":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/context-graph/README.md"},"name":"Write","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"49da723e6046dbccfcf0e3966f6e68a44a5964dd","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-12aea0d347ed43772459b525809c3fa69f94031c3b7316da0898ea91b1f46a50","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-4-8","type":"agent"},"session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code"},"occurred_at":"2026-07-19T17:25:31.204Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.2.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01V963HgseDFKxq4Tv8UC2bC","input":{"content":"# Context Graph\n\nA navigable graph of how everything in a repository connects — code, docs, and\nconversations, as one heterogeneous graph.\n\nMost of what a repository knows lives in the connections between its artifacts:\na file imports another, a doc explains a module, a conversation decides why a\nline is the way it is, a commit implements that decision. Those relationships\nexist but are never written down as first-class, addressable structure. Context\nGraph makes them explicit — typed edges, each traceable to the evidence that\njustifies it.\n\nThe first artifacts it wires up are **conversations**, because\n[Conversation Ledger](https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger)\nalready stores them durably and turnbridge already writes lineage edges into\nit. Code and doc nodes follow, sharing one identifier namespace so a\nconversation and the file it discusses are joinable.\n\nThis repository is intentionally at the design stage. Nothing here is locked\nin — it records current 