{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"File created successfully at: /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/README.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)","tool_use_id":"toolu_012dnRb8fNnZCA3L7qD9nQUN","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"49da723e6046dbccfcf0e3966f6e68a44a5964dd","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-7ad68b2f6d2bcbb1dde247b47c49a86dacbc36d5994d4cad36168d778e71d11f","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"type":"human"},"session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code"},"occurred_at":"2026-07-19T17:16:08.069Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.2.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"File created successfully at: /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/README.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)","tool_use_id":"toolu_012dnRb8fNnZCA3L7qD9nQUN","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"parentUuid":"2b4dd860-f2dc-4803-9c27-bbc3fdbca708","promptId":"5802adfd-dd29-4252-b8b0-ed28762a2d6d","sessionId":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","slug":"generic-stirring-candy","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2b4dd860-f2dc-4803-9c27-bbc3fdbca708","timestamp":"2026-07-19T17:16:08.069Z","toolUseResult":{"content":"# Conversation Graph\n\nDerive a navigable graph of how conversations connect — to each other and, in\ntime, to the code and docs they discuss.\n\nConversation Graph reads the durable record in\n[Conversation Ledger](https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger) and\nturns implicit relationships between conversations (a conversation bridged into\nanother CLI, one that supersedes an earlier decision, several that touch the\nsame files) into explicit, addressable edges. Its first consumer is a human\nasking \"how does this discussion relate to that one?\"; its second is a training\npipeline that traverses the graph.\n\nThis repository is intentionally at the design stage. Nothing here is locked\nin — it records current impressions and the shape of the problem, not a\ncommitted API. See [product intent](docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md) and the\n[WIP technical design](docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md).\n\n## Where it sits\n\n- **conversation-ledger** — neutral, immutable store of conversation events\n  (the source of truth this tool reads).\n- **turnbridge** — captures/moves conversations between CLIs; already writes\n  `continuation` lineage edges into the ledger that this tool would surface.\n- **intent-recall** — reads the ledger to answer \"what was intended?\"; a\n  sibling consumer, not a dependency.\n- **conversation-graph** (this repo) — reads the ledger, emits an explicit\n  relationship graph.\n- **[tagseq2tagseq](https://github.com/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq)** — trains\n  language models by traversing a text-attributed document graph; a natural\n  downstream consumer of the graph this tool emits (see the design doc).\n\n## License\n\n[MIT](LICENSE)\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/README.md","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"6d816c14-8c0e-40b4-864f-b1b934a8697a","version":"2.1.215"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-07-19T17:18:00.107Z","schema":"annals/v1","stream":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":838}}
{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"File created successfully at: /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)","tool_use_id":"toolu_01QNxb3AzTPEMGSdYfuH7AfX","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"49da723e6046dbccfcf0e3966f6e68a44a5964dd","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-dbf45e96739064f735960eb92c20844317217f3d32ec2686a443080673f7d822","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"type":"human"},"session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code"},"occurred_at":"2026-07-19T17:16:39.524Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.2.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"File created successfully at: /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)","tool_use_id":"toolu_01QNxb3AzTPEMGSdYfuH7AfX","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"parentUuid":"cc7280b5-8886-426e-abb8-a2fde0edac85","promptId":"5802adfd-dd29-4252-b8b0-ed28762a2d6d","sessionId":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","slug":"generic-stirring-candy","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cc7280b5-8886-426e-abb8-a2fde0edac85","timestamp":"2026-07-19T17:16:39.524Z","toolUseResult":{"content":"# Product intent\n\n**Status:** design-stage impressions. Nothing here is committed; it exists to\nframe the problem and record early opinions, and is expected to shift.\n\n## Purpose\n\nConversation Graph makes the relationships *between* conversations explicit and\naddressable. Conversation Ledger stores conversations as immutable events with\nenough provenance to reconstruct each one, but the connections among them —\nthis conversation continues that one in another CLI, this decision supersedes\nan earlier one, these three all edited the same file — live only implicitly in\ntimestamps, `links`, and shared context. This tool reads the ledger and\nproduces an explicit graph of those relationships that both a human and a\nmachine can traverse.\n\n## Behavioral commitments (intended)\n\n- Derive edges from evidence already in the ledger; never invent a relationship\n  the record does not support.\n- Keep every edge traceable back to the event(s) that justify it — a graph is a\n  derived view, and the raw record stays authoritative.\n- Treat the graph as rebuildable: it is an index over the ledger, not a second\n  source of truth, and re-deriving it from the same events yields the same\n  graph.\n- Distinguish edge *kinds* (continuation, supersession, shared-file,\n  same-author, temporal-adjacency, reference) rather than flattening everything\n  into one \"related\" link.\n- Make edge confidence and its basis visible, so a weak co-occurrence edge is\n  not mistaken for an explicit continuation.\n\n## Non-goals (for now)\n\n- Deciding which conversation is \"correct\" or ranking intent — that is\n  intent-recall's job; this tool supplies structure, not judgment.\n- Capturing conversations or moving them between CLIs — that is turnbridge.\n- Becoming a second store: the graph holds references and derived edges, not\n  copies of conversation content.\n\n## Relationship to the other tools\n\nConversation Graph is a **reader** of Conversation Ledger, a peer of\nintent-recall (both derive views from the ledger; neither depends on the\nother), and a **producer** for downstream consumers — most concretely\n[tagseq2tagseq](https://github.com/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq), whose training\npipeline traverses a text-attributed document graph. turnbridge already emits\n`continuation` lineage edges into the ledger; this tool is the first that reads\nthem as graph structure rather than as per-row labels.\n\n## The bigger idea (not this tool yet)\n\nThe same machinery generalizes past conversations to *every cross-file\nconnection in a repository* — code importing code, docs linking docs, a\nconversation that discusses a file, a commit that implements a decision — as\none heterogeneous graph. Whether that lives here or in a later sibling is\nundecided. It is called out in the technical design because it shapes the node\nand edge model even at this stage: the conversation graph should be a subgraph\nof that larger graph, not a differently-shaped thing that has to be rebuilt.\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"df9c6650-edd3-402d-bc64-8f843ea02da5","version":"2.1.215"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-07-19T17:18:00.107Z","schema":"annals/v1","stream":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":841}}
{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"File created successfully at: /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SwADR4dNwz2JnCYWCCTetZ","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"49da723e6046dbccfcf0e3966f6e68a44a5964dd","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-82a4f30c0c02c4cb4605ce0be0e0a48ffe4e33fd1dfb44269b3283bcf62b1497","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"type":"human"},"session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code"},"occurred_at":"2026-07-19T17:17:16.007Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.2.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"File created successfully at: /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SwADR4dNwz2JnCYWCCTetZ","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"parentUuid":"996f34a0-66e5-456b-92d4-329115141eb2","promptId":"5802adfd-dd29-4252-b8b0-ed28762a2d6d","sessionId":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","slug":"generic-stirring-candy","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"996f34a0-66e5-456b-92d4-329115141eb2","timestamp":"2026-07-19T17:17:16.007Z","toolUseResult":{"content":"# WIP technical design\n\n**Status:** exploratory impressions, nothing locked in — including the\nimplementation language. This records how the problem looks after building\nconversation-ledger and turnbridge, so later work does not start cold.\n\n## Inputs\n\nThe only required input is Conversation Ledger. Events are read through its\nlibrary API (`readEvents`, `sortEvents`) or `cledger export`, grouped by\n`conversation.id`. Everything needed to derive first-class edges is already\npresent:\n\n- `conversation.id` / `seq` — node identity and intra-conversation order.\n- `links` (e.g. `{rel:\"continues\", target}`) — turnbridge's `continuation`\n  lineage edges, and any future `supersession` links.\n- `actor.id` — author, for same-author edges.\n- `context.repo` / `branch` / `head` / `cwd` — repository grounding and, later,\n  the join key to code/doc nodes.\n- `occurred_at` — temporal adjacency.\n- content blocks — file paths mentioned in tool calls (`Read`, `Edit`, `Bash`),\n  which yield conversation→file edges once file nodes exist.\n\n## Node and edge model (draft)\n\n**Nodes** are conversations to start with: `{id, repo, author, first/last\nactivity, turn_count, title}`, referencing the ledger rather than copying\ncontent. The model is deliberately widened from day one so conversations are a\n*subgraph* of an eventual repo-wide graph — a node carries a `type`\n(`conversation` now; `file`, `commit`, `decision` later) and a stable\n`normalized_identifier`.\n\n**Edges** are typed and evidence-bearing: `{src, dst, kind, basis:[event_ids],\nconfidence}`. Candidate kinds:\n\n- `continuation` — from turnbridge `links`; explicit, high confidence.\n- `supersession` — a later decision overriding an earlier one (explicit when\n  linked; otherwise a candidate for intent-recall, not this tool, to assert).\n- `shared_file` — two conversations touched the same path.\n- `same_author` / `temporal_adjacency` — weak, co-occurrence edges; kept\n  clearly lower-confidence so they are not mistaken for explicit links.\n- `reference` — a conversation names another conversation/commit/file.\n\nExplicit edges (from `links`) are authoritative; derived edges (co-occurrence)\nalways carry their basis and a confidence so a consumer can filter.\n\n## Downstream target: tagseq2tagseq\n\ntagseq2tagseq trains on a **text-attributed document graph**. Its extractor\nlayer is three protocols — `ContentSource` (iterate `Document{identifier,\nnormalized_identifier, content, metadata}`), `LinkExtractor` (raw link targets\nfrom content), `LinkNormalizer` (canonical ids) — feeding a `GraphBuilder` that\nwrites `graph.jsonl`, one node per line with `outgoing`/`incoming` edge sets,\n`char_count`, and `metadata`, which the model then traverses (e.g. random\nwalk).\n\nThis tool should emit exactly that shape, so the conversation graph drops into\ntagseq2tagseq as a new `source_type`:\n\n- a conversation node → a `Document` whose `content` is its rendered transcript\n  (reuse turnbridge's literal-transcript renderer) and whose `normalized_id`\n  is the ledger `conversation.id`;\n- typed edges collapse into `outgoing`/`incoming` for training, but the richer\n  `{kind, basis, confidence}` is retained in `metadata` so nothing is lost;\n- alternatively, implement the conversation graph *as* a tagseq2tagseq\n  `ContentSource`+`LinkExtractor` pair rather than re-emitting JSONL. Which side\n  owns the adapter is open.\n\n## Generalization to a whole-repo graph\n\nThe larger ambition — graph every cross-file connection (code imports, doc\nlinks, conversation↔file, commit↔decision) — is the same `GraphBuilder` with\nmore extractors: one `ContentSource`/`LinkExtractor` per content type, sharing\none identifier namespace so a conversation node and the file it discusses are\njoinable. The conversation extractor is just the first. Keeping node identity\nand edge shape uniform now is what lets that compose later instead of forcing a\nrebuild. Whether the repo-wide graph lives here or in a later sibling is\nundecided; the design assumes it should be able to.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- **Language.** Reads TS (conversation-ledger) and feeds Python\n  (tagseq2tagseq). Emit neutral `graph.jsonl` from TS, or implement as a Python\n  tagseq2tagseq extractor, or split. Undecided.\n- **Storage.** Recompute the graph on demand (pure index) vs. persist it (and\n  if persisted, in git notes like the ledger, or a separate artifact).\n- **Cross-repo / cross-user.** The ledger can hold synced conversations from\n  collaborators; does the graph span repos, and how are identifiers namespaced\n  across them.\n- **Edge derivation ownership.** Which derived edges belong here vs. are left to\n  intent-recall to assert with its confidence machinery, to avoid two tools\n  claiming the same relationship differently.\n- **Rebuild determinism.** Guaranteeing the same events produce byte-identical\n  `graph.jsonl` (stable node/edge ordering) so the graph is diffable and\n  cacheable.\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-graph/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"31a62034-9eeb-43db-a248-3c22398ec700","version":"2.1.215"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-07-19T17:18:00.107Z","schema":"annals/v1","stream":{"id":"claude-code:c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","seq":845}}
