raph, not a differently-shaped thing that has to be rebuilt.\n","structuredPatch":[{"lines":[" "," ## Purpose"," ","-Conversation Graph makes the relationships *between* conversations explicit and","-addressable. Conversation Ledger stores conversations as immutable events with","-enough provenance to reconstruct each one, but the connections among them —","-this conversation continues that one in another CLI, this decision supersedes","-an earlier one, these three all edited the same file — live only implicitly in","-timestamps, `links`, and shared context. This tool reads the ledger and","-produces an explicit graph of those relationships that both a human and a","-machine can traverse.","+Context Graph makes the relationships *among a repository's artifacts* explicit","+and addressable. Code, docs, conversations, commits, and decisions are all","+partial expressions of the same work, densely connected — a file imports","+another, a doc explains a module, a conversation settles why a line exists, a","+commit implements that decision — but those connections are never recorded as","+first-class structure. This tool derives them into one typed graph that both a","+human and a machine can traverse."," ","+Conversations are the first artifact type wired up, because Conversation Ledger","+already stores them with enough provenance to reconstruct each one and","+turnbridge already writes `continuation` lineage edges into it. Code and doc","+nodes follow. The graph is heterogeneous from the start so those later nodes","+join the same structure rather than forcing a rebuild.","+"," ## Behavioral commitments (intended)"," ","-- Derive edges from evidence already in the ledger; never invent a relationship","-  the record does not support.","-- Keep every edge traceable back to the event(s) that justify it — a graph is a","-  derived view, and the raw record stays authoritative.","-- Treat the graph as rebuildable: it is an index over the ledger, not a second","-  source of truth, and re-deriving it from the same events yields the same","-  graph.","-- Distinguish edge *kinds* (continuation, supersession, shared-file,","-  same-author, temporal-adjacency, reference) rather than flattening everything","-  into one \"related\" link.","+- Derive edges from evidence that already exists (ledger events, import","+  statements, doc links, commit metadata); never invent a relationship the","+  artifacts do not support.","+- Keep every edge traceable back to what justifies it — a graph is a derived","+  view, and the underlying artifacts stay authoritative.","+- Treat the graph as rebuildable: it is an index over the repository and its","+  ledger, not a second source of truth; re-deriving from the same inputs yields","+  the same graph.","+- Distinguish edge *kinds* (continuation, supersession, imports, documents,","+  discusses, implements, shared-file, same-author, temporal) rather than","+  flattening everything into one \"related\" link."," - Make edge confidence and its basis visible, so a weak co-occurrence edge is","-  not mistaken for an explicit continuation.","+  not mistaken for an explicit reference."," "," ## Non-goals (for now)"," ","-- Deciding which conversation is \"correct\" or ranking intent — that is","+- Deciding which artifact is \"correct\" or ranking intent — that is","   intent-recall's job; this tool supplies structure, not judgment."," - Capturing conversations or moving them between CLIs — that is turnbridge.","-- Becoming a second store: the graph holds references and derived edges, not","-  copies of conversation content.","+- Becoming a second store: nodes reference artifacts and hold derived edges,","+  not copies of their content."," "," ## Relationship to the other tools"," ","-Conversation Graph is a **reader** of Conversation Ledger, a peer of","-intent-recall (both derive views from the ledger; neither depends on the","-other), and a **producer** for downstream consumers — most concretely","+Context Graph is