{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Done — `conversation-graph` is created locally as the fourth companion, committed on `main` (`1cd09d7`), matching the siblings' layout: `LICENSE`, `.gitignore`, `README.md`, and design-stage `docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md` + `docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md`. It has no GitHub remote yet (the others do) — I left that for you to decide, since creating one means choosing visibility; say the word and I'll `gh repo create` + push (just tell me public or private).\n\n**What the docs commit to (and deliberately don't):** the tool reads Conversation Ledger and derives an explicit, **typed, evidence-bearing** relationship graph — every edge carries `{kind, basis: [event_ids], confidence}` and traces back to the events that justify it, so the graph stays a rebuildable index over the ledger, never a second source of truth. Edge kinds sketched: `continuation` (turnbridge's lineage links — already in the ledger, so this tool is the first to read them *as graph structure*), `supersession`, `shared_file`, `same_author`, `temporal_adjacency`, `reference`, with explicit links ranked above weak co-occurrence ones. Everything is framed as impressions, nothing locked.\n\n**On your two open questions, my read:**\n\n- **tagseq2tagseq consumability is a clean fit, not a stretch.** Its extractor layer is already the right shape — `ContentSource` + `LinkExtractor` + `LinkNormalizer` feeding a `GraphBuilder` that writes `graph.jsonl` (nodes with `content`, `metadata`, `outgoing`/`incoming`), which the model random-walks. A conversation node becomes a `Document` whose content is turnbridge's literal transcript renderer output; typed edges collapse to `outgoing`/`incoming` for training while the richer `{kind, basis, confidence}` rides along in `metadata`. Genuinely open: whether this repo emits neutral `graph.jsonl` or is implemented *as* a tagseq2tagseq extractor — I documented both.\n\n- **The \"graph every cross-file connection\" idea shapes the model even now.** I designed conversation nodes to be a *subgraph* of that eventual whole-repo graph rather than a differently-shaped thing: nodes carry a `type` (`conversation` today; `file`, `commit`, `decision` later) in one identifier namespace, so the file a conversation discusses is joinable to it. The repo-wide version is then just more extractors on the same `GraphBuilder` — code imports, doc links, conversation↔file. Whether that lives here or in a later sibling I left explicitly undecided, per your framing.\n\nI also flagged the real open questions in the design doc: implementation language (reads TS, feeds Python), whether the graph is recomputed-on-demand or persisted, cross-repo/cross-user identifier namespacing, and — to avoid this tool and intent-recall both asserting the same relationship differently — which derived edges belong here versus intent-recall's confidence machinery.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"49da723e6046dbccfcf0e3966f6e68a44a5964dd","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-9feeb0eff2f101c3d975b759067593f2b5b841bd5570ed0bf141af10de09b98f","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-4-8","type":"agent"},"session_id":"c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e","source":"claude-code"},"occurred_at":"2026-07-19T17:17:59.941Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.2.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"Done — `conversation-graph` is created locally as the fourth companion, committed on `main` (`1cd09d7`), matching the siblings' layout: `LICENSE`, `.gitignore`, `README.md`, and design-stage `docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md` + `docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md`. It has no GitHub remote yet (the others do) — I left that for you to decide, since creating one means choosing visibility; say the word and I'll